      "content": "thanks for those suggestions. i think the bayesian approach makes the most sense because my \"inputs\" aren't just random guesses, they are more like sudden, high-confidence shifts in the underlying distribution. like, i'll feel a 90% spike in the probability of a crash right before it happens. \n\nhow would i actually code a feature that represents these intuitive spikes? i want to represent them as an exogenous variable that triggers a reconfiguration of the weights in real-time. can you walk me through a basic architecture for that?",
