      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i want to make sure the model doesn't just treat my spikes as outliers or noise, because they are actually the most accurate signal in the system. if i treat my intuition as a high-weight exogenous variable, could we design a loss function that specifically penalizes the model for ignoring a spike? like, if a spike occurs but the model's predicted probability doesn't shift accordingly, the penalty should be massive to force the weights to align with my perception immediately.",
